<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-b2b-buyers-2026-10-11-rebap-2024-vol-weighted-226-eur-mwh-short-26> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#relatedTo> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-b2b-buyers-2026-10-11-rebap-2024-vol-weighted-226-eur-mwh-short-26> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#hasDomain> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-b2b-buyers-2026-10-11-rebap-2024-vol-weighted-226-eur-mwh-short-26> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#createdAt> "2026-10-11T17:08:26Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-b2b-buyers-2026-10-11-rebap-2024-vol-weighted-226-eur-mwh-short-26> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#status> "active" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-b2b-buyers-2026-10-11-rebap-2024-vol-weighted-226-eur-mwh-short-26> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteType> "insight" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-b2b-buyers-2026-10-11-rebap-2024-vol-weighted-226-eur-mwh-short-26> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "Track DE B2B buyers (2026-10-11): reBAP 2024 vol-weighted +226 EUR/MWh short / -26 long, max 15,000; TSO AEP estimator at T+30min has MAE 3.07 EUR/MWh (Q1 2026) so post-hoc reBAP prediction is worthless; value is pre-gate-closure NRV-sign forecasting and own forecast-error reduction (own estimate 15-40k EUR/yr per 100 GWh supplier, 150-400k per TWh). No published Stadtwerk imbalance cost; no Stadtwerke forecasting tenders found; EU sector threshold 432k so pilots are direct awards. Cooperatives centralise forecasting (Trianel 53 Stadtwerke, 138 TWh, in-house AI; Syneco/Thuega Munich; Suedweststrom). Direktvermarkter top: Quadra 10.1 GW, EnBW 9.9, Next 8.0; 29/46 have battery books. Large BESS 2.5 GW end-2025 -> ~5 GW end-2026; aFRR-prequalified batteries 0.56->1.20 GW; revenue ~132-155k EUR/MW/yr 2026. All optimiser public references >=20 MW: 100 kW-5 MW C&I is an underserved hypothesis. No paid DSO flex market in DE 2026. enspired pre-sold before code, first customer a pumped-storage operator; suena/Entrix first references via IPPs/municipals not tenders. Munich-reachable candidates: Entrix, Kyon (Iberian angle), Stadtwerke Rosenheim, Syneco/Thuega, ESB, N-ERGIE, mid-sized DVs." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-b2b-buyers-2026-10-11-rebap-2024-vol-weighted-226-eur-mwh-short-26> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#Note> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-data-quant-2026-10-11-smard-dwd-ecmwf-open-data-mastr-e-redes-open-data> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#relatedTo> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-data-quant-2026-10-11-smard-dwd-ecmwf-open-data-mastr-e-redes-open-data> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#hasDomain> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-data-quant-2026-10-11-smard-dwd-ecmwf-open-data-mastr-e-redes-open-data> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#createdAt> "2026-10-11T17:06:49Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-data-quant-2026-10-11-smard-dwd-ecmwf-open-data-mastr-e-redes-open-data> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#status> "active" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-data-quant-2026-10-11-smard-dwd-ecmwf-open-data-mastr-e-redes-open-data> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteType> "insight" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-data-quant-2026-10-11-smard-dwd-ecmwf-open-data-mastr-e-redes-open-data> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "Track data/quant (2026-10-11): SMARD, DWD, ECMWF open data, MaStR, E-REDES open data (70 datasets, hourly consumption by postal code) are CC BY 4.0 / commercial-OK; Energy-Charts day-ahead prices are private-use only for most zones; Open-Meteo Previous Runs API (~USD 99/mo) is the only clean no-look-ahead weather source; REN Data Hub exposes no desvios/reserve prices (partner needed); OMIE/ESIOS licence unverified. reBAP published ~20 working days after month; AEP estimator at T+30min. HTW Berlin 2026: price-optimised control saves 233 EUR/yr without PV but only 64 EUR/yr with PV+battery; Modul 1+3 grid-fee relief dominates. MPC captures 50-90% of perfect-foresight arbitrage. German DA spread ~30 (2019) -> ~130 EUR/MWh (2024); Iberian BESS DA benchmark ~130k EUR/MW (2025). Three experiment designs specified in the note." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-data-quant-2026-10-11-smard-dwd-ecmwf-open-data-mastr-e-redes-open-data> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#Note> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-at-ch-uk-nordics-2026-10-11-austria-has-5-590-eegs-1-000-begs-500k> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#relatedTo> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-at-ch-uk-nordics-2026-10-11-austria-has-5-590-eegs-1-000-begs-500k> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#hasDomain> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-at-ch-uk-nordics-2026-10-11-austria-has-5-590-eegs-1-000-begs-500k> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#createdAt> "2026-10-11T17:06:18Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-at-ch-uk-nordics-2026-10-11-austria-has-5-590-eegs-1-000-begs-500k> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#status> "active" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-at-ch-uk-nordics-2026-10-11-austria-has-5-590-eegs-1-000-begs-500k> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteType> "insight" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-at-ch-uk-nordics-2026-10-11-austria-has-5-590-eegs-1-000-begs-500k> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "Track AT/CH/UK/Nordics (2026-10-11): Austria has 5,590 EEGs + ~1,000 BEGs, ~500k metering points, 96.9% smart meters with 15-min data next day, grid-fee discounts 28-57%; ElWG community rules from 1 Oct 2026 but SNE-VO discounts only 1 Jan 2027. Community platform vendors (Exnaton 50+ utilities, neoom, eFriends, 7Energy, OurPower) do no forecasting: plausible API wedge, unproven. APG reserves tiny (FCR 75 MW), enspired dominant optimiser. Switzerland: deprioritise until 2027+. UK/Nordic lesson: reserve markets of a few hundred MW saturate in ~18 months, per-asset revenue halves in 2 years (SE FCR-D 30-60 -> <3 EUR/MWh; CheckWatt ~EUR 500/battery/yr minus 25% fee); software take ~25% of a declining number; venture case needs >=100k assets or a platform licence model." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-at-ch-uk-nordics-2026-10-11-austria-has-5-590-eegs-1-000-begs-500k> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#Note> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-hardware-control-2026-10-11-no-proprietary-hardware-needed-for-viable> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#relatedTo> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-hardware-control-2026-10-11-no-proprietary-hardware-needed-for-viable> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#hasDomain> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-hardware-control-2026-10-11-no-proprietary-hardware-needed-for-viable> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#createdAt> "2026-10-11T17:04:31Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-hardware-control-2026-10-11-no-proprietary-hardware-needed-for-viable> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#status> "active" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-hardware-control-2026-10-11-no-proprietary-hardware-needed-for-viable> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteType> "insight" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-hardware-control-2026-10-11-no-proprietary-hardware-needed-for-viable> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "Track hardware/control (2026-10-11): no proprietary hardware needed for viable wedges. Most 2020+ hybrid inverters expose local Modbus/SunSpec control (Enphase, Varta, Solarwatt, old sonnen read-only); HTW 2026: grid-charge round-trip <=78%, spread must be >=14 ct/kWh at 60% efficiency; DE 10 kWh home battery arbitrage gross 50/120/250 EUR/yr. C&I 1MW/2MWh DE index fell 309k->259k EUR/MW/yr 2024->2025, ~155-200k in 2026; FCR saturated; Spain comparator 477k (Jul 2026). V2G is OEM-locked bundles (BMW+E.ON, VW/Elli, cap 720 EUR/yr); V1G ~164 EUR/car/yr, 440 with s14a modules. CLS/Steuerbox is a DSO curtailment path not a dispatch channel. Cheapest control paths: C&I via direct marketer/EMS, V1G via OCPP/telematics, residential via HEMS partner (gridX)." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-hardware-control-2026-10-11-no-proprietary-hardware-needed-for-viable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#Note> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-nl-be-2026-10-11-dutch-household-imbalance-trading-is-real-but> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#relatedTo> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-nl-be-2026-10-11-dutch-household-imbalance-trading-is-real-but> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#hasDomain> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-nl-be-2026-10-11-dutch-household-imbalance-trading-is-real-but> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#createdAt> "2026-10-11T17:04:19Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-nl-be-2026-10-11-dutch-household-imbalance-trading-is-real-but> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#status> "active" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-nl-be-2026-10-11-dutch-household-imbalance-trading-is-real-but> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteType> "insight" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-nl-be-2026-10-11-dutch-household-imbalance-trading-is-real-but> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "Track NL/BE (2026-10-11): Dutch household imbalance trading is real but compressing (Mijnbatterij 2026: EUR 74-178 per 10 kW/month; Frank Energie EUR 1,298/yr hybrid vs 841 EPEX-only), steering is contract-locked to suppliers, TenneT regeltoestand-2 share ~40% in 2026 and rule churn ahead; software wedge is B2B imbalance/regeltoestand forecasting for BRPs, already occupied by Dexter Energy (EUR 23m Series C Jul 2025). NL = credible second market, BE = third. Neither is a first market." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-nl-be-2026-10-11-dutch-household-imbalance-trading-is-real-but> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#Note> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-small-asset-2026-10-11-household-vpp-aggregation-in-germany-is-closed> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#relatedTo> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-small-asset-2026-10-11-household-vpp-aggregation-in-germany-is-closed> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#hasDomain> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#domain/research> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-small-asset-2026-10-11-household-vpp-aggregation-in-germany-is-closed> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#createdAt> "2026-10-11T17:02:33Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-small-asset-2026-10-11-household-vpp-aggregation-in-germany-is-closed> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#status> "active" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-small-asset-2026-10-11-household-vpp-aggregation-in-germany-is-closed> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteType> "insight" <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-small-asset-2026-10-11-household-vpp-aggregation-in-germany-is-closed> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "Track DE small-asset (2026-10-11): household VPP/aggregation in Germany is closed to software-only outsiders (no device access, no meter, no Bilanzkreis; Enpal/1KOMMA5/sonnen/Tibber/Octopus vertically integrated and now selling their stacks). Only 5.9% of metering points had iMSys at 30 Jun 2026 (BNetzA). Passive balancing is not permitted in DE. Plausible wedge: reBAP-exposure/forecast-error reduction for second-tier BKVs (regional suppliers, Stadtwerke, small Direktvermarkter)." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-de-small-asset-2026-10-11-household-vpp-aggregation-in-germany-is-closed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#Note> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
