<http://ops-sys.local/ontology#note/track-competition-precedents-2026-10-11-big-residential-players-1komma5-enpal> <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#noteText> "Track competition/precedents (2026-10-11): big residential players (1KOMMA5, Enpal, Kraken) are platform sellers not buyers; only outside-intelligence case is Enpal-Entrix JV. Grid-scale optimisers well funded (Entrix EUR 43m Mar 2026, enspired >EUR 40m, Flexpower sold to Citadel Oct 2025, suena EUR 8m Series A); Kyon dual-sources optimisers. Forecast vendor licences EUR 2-25k/yr per portfolio; Stadtwerke still Excel+experience, vendors win via 6-12 month parallel runs. 16 precedents: time-to-first-revenue 1-6 months with a trading partner, 2-3+ years software-only; pure model shops exited as trade sales (PowerBot/Likron->Volue, Nnergix->Circutor). Realistic entry: sub-supplier of 15-min PV/wind, imbalance-price or co-located dispatch models to an existing optimiser/direct marketer on performance share; Iberian beachhead via E-REDES/Piclo live DSO flex + German optimisers entering ES/PT. Avoid direct residential VPP, standalone Stadtwerke forecasting, principal BESS optimisation." <http://ops-sys.local/ontology#graph/ws/energy> .
